# desktop-min.pkgs — the tier for a machine with about a gigabyte.
#
# IceWM rather than XFCE, and that is the whole difference between this tier and
# the next: XFCE's session, panel, settings daemon and file manager are four
# resident processes before anything is opened. IceWM is one, it themes to look
# like the era of the hardware it is running on, and it has a menu, a taskbar and
# a window list, which is the whole of what a desktop has to have.
#
# ⚠ xorg-minimal, NOT xorg. `xorg` is a metapackage that pulls every video driver
# in the tree plus fonts nobody asked for; on this tier that is most of the disk.
# Drivers are named per architecture instead.
xorg-minimal
xorg-fonts
xf86-input-libinput
xinit
icewm
xterm
pcmanfm
gvfs
gvfs-mtp
alsa-utils
alsa-plugins
feh
dillo
xarchiver
